{"availability":"available","full":"richrd/heart-rate-monitor","name":"heart-rate-monitor","description":"💓 A web based heart rate monitor that measures pulse from the fingertip using the phone camera.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":144,"forks":28,"created":"2021-01-09T15:31:20Z","updated":"2021-03-12T17:33:24Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://heartrate.netlify.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://heartrate.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:33:43.502Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:33:43.502Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:33:43.502Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T21:08:06.033Z","stars":144,"forks":28},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:33:43.502Z","stars":144,"forks":28}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A web based heart rate monitor that measures pulse from the fingertip using the phone camera. It works the same way as many camera based heart rate monitor apps, but it works entirely in the browser so nothing needs to be installed on your phone. At the moment it's recomended to use it on Chrome since other browsers don't yet support turning on the torch.","I wanted a phone based heart rate monitor app, but I didn't feel like installing some random ad infested tracking ridden app from the app store. So I set out to see if I could pull this off with web tech only. I knew there were three things I needed to implement this:","Aa brief web search confirmed that all of that was possible, so I wrote a quick and dirty prototype. The prototype was promising so I polished the code and gave it a nice app-like UI. Since the app is entirely client side I intentionally decided to leave out any frameworks, libraries and build processes. Writing vanilla HTML, CSS and JS was actually very refreshing for a change. As an added benefit deploying it is simply a matter of serving the src directory over HTTP. I will also never face broken dependencies on this project :)"],"features":["Accessing a video stream from the camera of the phone","Sampling pixel data from the frames of the video stream","Turning on the flash light of the phone to get a consistent brightness level (seems to work on chrome only)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/richrd/heart-rate-monitor/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9a7227b7dea4685491560f72adb75e6228fa3e20a926e7c69179bc51956a7179","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:06.206Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:06.206Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A web based heart rate monitor that measures pulse from the fingertip using the phone camera. It works the same way as many camera based heart rate monitor apps, but it works entirely in the browser so nothing needs to be installed on your phone. At the moment it's recomended to use it on Chrome since other browsers don't yet support turning on the torch.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/richrd/heart-rate-monitor/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"9a7227b7dea4685491560f72adb75e6228fa3e20a926e7c69179bc51956a7179","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/richrd/heart-rate-monitor/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:06.206Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2021-03-12T17:33:24Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/richrd/heart-rate-monitor/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:06.207Z","hash":"9a7227b7dea4685491560f72adb75e6228fa3e20a926e7c69179bc51956a7179","originalBytes":3426,"storedBytes":3426,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["app","heart","monitor","rate","phone","works","based","chrome","currently","flash","measurement.","only","out","stable","things","web","when","work","added","average","bpm","camera","camera.","entirely","even","fft","find","finger","first","graph","like","make","measurement","measures","needs","possible","screenshot","see","service","should","since","some","stream","there","time","try","turning","using","video","want","way","worker",